    - name: Get Local Player's Screen Name
      description: 'Unfortunately, the next child object can have different names,
        so we can''t do a find on it. Instead, we use "Get Child Num" to get the
        first child, regardless of name.


        Then, we can use a "Get Child"
        to find ''NameText" gameObject.


        Once we have that, we get the "Text"
        script component, and finally get the "Text.text" value, which contains the
        local player

        s name. Whew!'
